  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...    \nFlat ridging/quasi-zonal flow will briefly settle over the SW Conus \nWednesday before another pronounced trough with strong cyclonic flow \npropagates inland from the East Pacific late in the week. Ensemble \nagreement is excellent maintaining the bulk of the negative height \nanomaly and cold core well into central/northern California and \nNevada. As such, the jet core should only descend into northern \nArizona keeping the forecast area under a more anti-cyclonic \nsubsident regime. Some moisture may be entrained along a decaying \ncold front Thursday night/Friday, though orographics will likely \ncontribute the greatest towards focused ascent. Given this scenario, \nPOPs are only highlighted in higher terrain areas with minimal QPF. \nRegardless, this trough passage will reinforce temperatures 3F-6F \nbelow normal through the weekend with unusually good confidence \ngiven narrow spread of numerical guidance uncharacteristic for 5 \ndays in advance during the passage of a weather system. Ensemble \nvariations grow substantially late in the weekend due to the \ninteraction of Pacific energy with an enhanced subtropical jet. \nWhile the operational GFS and a handful of GEFS members suggest \nanother deepening trough entering the SW Conus, this solution is \nmore of a minority versus the entire NAEFS suite with the ensemble \nmean favoring only inconsequential broad cyclonic, or quasi-zonal \nflow towards the end of this forecast period.",
